# Architecture — Feature-based Clean Arch + MVI

## Package layout

Root: `com.balius.galius`

```
core/                 # app-wide infra only (no feature UI)
  di/
  network/
  database/
  navigation/
  mvi/                # shared MVI base types

common/               # shared by ≥2 features
  ui/
  model/
  util/

feature/
  {featureName}/
    data/
      repository/     # implementations
      local/
      remote/
    domain/
      model/
      repository/     # interfaces only
      usecase/
    presentation/
      {Feature}Screen.kt
      {Feature}ViewModel.kt
      {Feature}Intent.kt
      {Feature}State.kt
      {Feature}Effect.kt
      {Feature}Reducer.kt
      components/
```

Keep existing `MainActivity` at root and Material theme under `ui/theme/` (or `common/ui/theme` if moved later).

## Layer rules

- **core**: DI, DB, network, navigation, MVI base. Never feature screens or feature domain.
- **common**: only code used by 2+ features. Prefer feature-local until shared need is clear.
- **feature**: vertical slice. New screens/features live under `feature/{name}/`.
- Dependencies: `presentation` → `domain` ← `data`. Domain never imports data or presentation.
- Features must not import another feature’s `data` or `presentation`. Share via `common` or `domain` contracts in `core` when needed.
- Data implements domain repository interfaces.

## MVI + reducer

Per feature presentation:

| Type | Role |
|------|------|
| `State` | Immutable UI state |
| `Intent` | User/system events |
| `Effect` | One-shot side effects (nav, snackbar) — not in State |
| `Reducer` | Pure: `(State, Intent) → State` (and/or effect signals) |
| `ViewModel` | Holds state, maps intents, runs use cases, applies reducer, emits effects |
| `Screen` | Compose UI: collect state, send intents, handle effects |

Rules:

- UI never mutates state directly — only sends `Intent`.
- Business logic in `domain` (use cases); reducer stays pure (no IO, no Android).
- Suspend/async work in ViewModel / use cases, then reduce result intents (e.g. `LoadSuccess`, `LoadError`).
- Prefer sealed interfaces for `Intent`, `Effect`, and loading/error variants in `State`.

## When adding code

1. Put it in the correct `feature/{name}/{layer}` (or `core` / `common`).
2. Do not dump feature code into root or `ui/` except theme / app entry.
3. New UI composables → feature `presentation` (+ `@Preview` per project preview rule).
4. Match existing naming: `{Feature}State`, `{Feature}Intent`, `{Feature}Reducer`, etc.
